  "summary": {
    "as": "Introduced in House",
    "asOf": "2025-06-25",
    "date": "2026-10-05T19:54:33Z",
    "text": "EQIP Improvement Act of 2025\n\nThis bill modifies payment limitations and reduces the federal cost share for certain projects authorized under the Environmental Quality Incentives Program (EQIP).\u00a0As background, this Department of Agriculture program provides technical and financial assistance to agricultural producers and forest landowners to address natural resource concerns.\n\nSpecifically, the bill\u00a0limits the total payments available to a person or legal entity under EQIP to $150,000 over a specified five-year period. (A $450,000 statutory\u00a0limit was in effect for FY2019-FY2024, and a regulatory contract limit of $450,000 currently applies.)\n\nThe bill also reduces the maximum federal cost share to 40% (from 75%) for the costs associated with planning, installation, or maintenance for specified conservation practices (e.g., access roads, dams, and waste storage facilities)."
  },
